  "topic": "bronze_age",
  "ttsScript": "In 1177 BC, every major civilization collapsed at the same time. Textbooks blame the Sea Peoples — raiders who burned everything. Nobody knows who they were. Hittites. Mycenaeans. Egyptians. Babylonians. All fell within fifty years. Every empire depended on the others. Tin from Afghanistan. Copper from Cyprus. Grain from Egypt. One break and everything starved. Writing disappeared for 400 years. A system so connected that when one part failed, everything fell. Sound familiar?",
